        en: [
          '**Semiconservative DNA replication**, demonstrated by **Meselson and Stahl (1958)** using $^{15}\\text{N}/^{14}\\text{N}$ density-gradient centrifugation, ensures that each daughter DNA duplex retains one parental template strand paired with one newly synthesized strand.',
          'At the **replication fork**, hexameric **DNA helicase** hydrolyzes ATP to unwind the double helix while **topoisomerase** relieves torsional supercoiling ahead of the fork. Because **DNA Polymerase III** catalyzes nucleophilic attack of the $3\'\\text{-OH}$ terminus on incoming $\\text{dNTPs}$, chain elongation proceeds exclusively in the **$5\' \\to 3\'$ direction**.',
          'Consequently, the antiparallel duplex imposes asymmetric synthesis: the **leading strand** elongates continuously toward the advancing fork on the $3\' \\to 5\'$ template, whereas the **lagging strand** is synthesized discontinuously away from the fork as short **Okazaki fragments** initiated by RNA primers, processed by DNA Polymerase I, and sealed by **DNA ligase**.'
        ]
